Z||000000||Monkeyman||11-26-1999||09:31 PM||||Just found an interior sunroof shade on eBay.  The auction ends at 6am PST.  Current price is $203.50.  I've heard that these are fairly rare.  I'd bid on it but don't have the money.  <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=204236486" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=204236486</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Patrick||11-26-1999||11:37 PM||||<BR>I never knew such things existed. Good idea, although the price seems awfully high. For the amount of sun we get in Vancouver, it wouldn't be worthwhile... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-26-1999||11:51 PM||||I hadn't heard about them, either, until about 3 weeks ago.  Another Fiero owner said that they were rare.  Probably true as I've never seen one.  You're right.  Lots of money.  I live in Indiana so I see lots of sun, but my sunroof is tinted, so I don't think I'll worry about it.  Besides, I think I could make one if I really felt like I had to have one.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-27-1999||12:28 AM||||I beleive that's Paul Vargas selling it. The e-mail matches what my files have for him. He sells allot of assorted parts. I don't know much about him. Wouldn't suprise me if he was one of our readers that's not registered. He is or was involved fairly heavily with one of the clubs. I forget which.<P>That's a hell of allot of money for it. Must be some show freak doing a resto to bid that much for it.<P>As for me there are a few times that the sun comes in at an odd angle and gets annoying, but my roof is open so much that a shade would only sit in the bag forever. If I understand right, the shade gets installed by seperating the roof latch and sits in the gap between the interior trim and glass. The square cutout fits the lip on the latch bracket. I think you can open the glass with the shade in, but mine gets opened even in the rain quite a bit and it's out every chance I get. ((for me at least, very little rain gets in unless it's a down pour, even when the car is stopped.))<P>I don't know about some of the earlier cars, but the later glass is all slightly mirrored as well as heavy tinted. I found this summer that throwing a 6$ reflective screen in the windscreen was more effective heat wise than covering the roof.<P>BTW.... for our new owners..... Be extremely carefull taking out the roof glass in hot weather. It gets increadibly hot. Hotter than any other glass on the car. It can easily get to many degrees above air temp. Did I say it get's hot yet? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||11-27-1999||12:59 AM||||With the help of a fellow member I acquired a sunshade to copy and make them available with bags for all at a reasonable price.||||reg||1
Z||000005||87FieroGT||11-27-1999||02:42 AM||||I made one out of some left over headliner and some panel board I bought from the local fabric company. Total cost was about $10 dollars. I just made a template out of cardboard and then traced it on to the panel board. I them used contact cement and glued on the headliner. Looks like it was made from the factory.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||11-27-1999||04:49 AM||||Car cover does the trick! Protects the outside as well.||||reg||12
Z||000007||TOM||11-27-1999||11:32 AM||||All of you do know about the wind deflector that goes with the sunroof, right?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Earne||11-27-1999||11:56 AM||||Just bought the sunroof screen from Paul V.  Indeed they are rare and it will increase the value of my 86.5 GT.  I show the car frequently and I have always been a little jealous of the few I have seen at the shows.  No one has ever even considered selling one.||||reg||10
Z||000009||theogre||11-27-1999||11:58 AM||||I have 2 deflectors.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> that way if I forget to take it off when I run in the store and some goof ball swipes it I still have one.<P>The deflectors are fairly easy to find. Most people don't seem to use them so they hardly ever get pulled out of the rack.||||reg||1
Z||000010||88formula||11-27-1999||03:27 PM||||I've got one of those, its just a piece of headliner.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fiero56||11-28-1999||08:09 PM||||I got a shade and the bag when I bought my Fiero in February.  The guy said he had a insert for the sunshade if I wanted it.  "Sure" I said, had no idea how rare they were.  We went up and searched his attick for about 15-20 minutes before we found it.  It was still sealed in it's original plastic bag from GM.  Too bad I opened it up to see what the insert looked like.  The guy said he just stuck it in his attick because he had no use for it, so it had been in there since he bought the car new back in '88. It's still in brand new condition, the little velvro dots are still unused.||||reg||1
