Z||000018||Monkeyman||11-30-1999||01:12 PM||||Dogtired--The bags Rodney Dickman sells are for show only.  The sunroof covers won't fit in the bags.  He recommends cutting a piece of cardboard to fit inside.  <BR>Jim Goose--They weren't exotic.  Apparently, they just didn't make many of them or else everyone took them out and lost them.  I've admired Fieros since before they were produced and I'd never seen one until the one on eBay. <BR>Tom--How much for one?  I don't need one, but if the price is right it might be cool to have one.  And you really do need to send us a list of all of the items you carry with prices.||||reg||1
Z||000019||TOM||11-30-1999||05:47 PM||||First off let me say thank you guys. Without you I wouldn't be who I am. And second why make a bag that is too small? I dont get it. And here is my site. Its small but coming along. <A HREF="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/tomfiero/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/tomfiero/</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||theogre||11-30-1999||06:41 PM||||The bag rodney has is actually from a diferant application, and is just labled for fiero as far as I remember. I don't see the point either. As someone who used to show a couple cars, I find that sort of thing annoying.||||reg||1
Z||000021||fiero56||11-30-1999||09:22 PM||||If I remember it correctly Rodney used an original Fiero insert bag, but the one he used as it turned out, had shrunk from heat and distorted.  He didn't discover this until the bags had been made up.  He is selling the smaller ones at a lower price and then will make them the correct size. I don't mind him making these bags, but I do wish people wouldn't pass them off as O.E. at car shows etc.  Rodney should super glue a bright orange tag on the back stating: "This bag is a reproduction and is not original equipment from a Feiro..." I would be a little happier.<BR>It does help those people who have the insert and no bag, if they want to keep the insert clean.||||reg||1
Z||000022||87GT||11-30-1999||11:08 PM||||I just now decided to look at this post and didnt realize that that piece is rare.  I have that piece to my sunroof.  The previous owner said that he couldnt find the bag to it when he sold me the car, so rats!  I usually have it in because it really reduces the whistling sound when the sunroof is down and your going down the road.  But, the others that have it are right, it isnt anything special.||||reg||1
Z||000023||RossT||11-30-1999||11:56 PM||||The original window sticker for my 88gt indicates that the sunshade is included with<BR>the sunroof option. Mine just sits in my trunk. I don't think I would part with it though. It would be a nice thing to show the<BR>judges at a show.<P>Ross||||reg||1
